138	114,471,557,1620	138. Terminal Flower.	A whole Trillium plant: a thick rootstock with fibrous roots, a single bare stem, a whorl of three broad leaves, and one three-petalled flower at the summit.
139	1325,843,1650,1616	139. Axillary Flowers.	A leafy stem of Moneywort with roundish leaves in pairs and single open flowers and buds on stalks from the axils of the leaves.
